---
title: Cross-Border Remote Work & Permanent Establishment Tax Advisory
sourceType: statutory_statute
date: 2025-06-01
jurisdiction: Global
language: en
register: statutory_legal
format: pdf
---

Employees working remotely outside their contracting country for more than 183 days within any twelve-month period create immediate permanent establishment tax liabilities for the employer.

Working remotely from an unauthorized foreign jurisdiction without an active social security A1 certificate exposes the company to mandatory back-payments under EU Regulation 883/2004.

Remote work abroad is strictly prohibited without prior written sign-off from both Corporate Tax and Legal Counsel.
